1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,587
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:06,673
[gunshots]

3
00:00:06,756 --> 00:00:07,966
[gun clicks, fires]

4
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:10,677
[whoosh, slashing sounds]

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,679
[machine gun fire]

6
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:14,681
[machine gun fire continues]

7
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:15,765
[single gunshot]

8
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:19,853
[rapid gunfire]

9
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:22,397
[echoing blast]

10
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,107
[rapid gunfire]

11
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:25,942
[blade whooshing]

12
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:28,445
[tense music builds]

13
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,696
[blade whooshing]

14
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:34,909
[Arnaldo] <i>It's just us now!</i>

15
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:37,829
<i>You're mine! You're all mine!</i>

16
00:00:37,912 --> 00:00:39,289
[Diego] <i>Get your hands off my wife!</i>

17
00:00:39,372 --> 00:00:44,252
[Lily] <i>As long as you live,</i>
<i>no one will ever love you, Arnaldo!</i>

18
00:00:44,335 --> 00:00:46,546
<i>No one! Because you're a monster!</i>

19
00:00:46,629 --> 00:00:49,382
<i>Even if you let me live,</i>
<i>I will never love you!</i>

20
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:51,134
<i>I will never love you!</i>

21
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:52,886
<i>I will never love a criminal!</i>

22
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:54,888
-[screams]
-[gunshot]

23
00:00:54,971 --> 00:00:57,932
[Julio] <i>Blood will be paid with blood.</i>

24
00:00:58,016 --> 00:00:59,851
<i>I promise you that, Arnaldo.</i>

25
00:00:59,934 --> 00:01:00,769
<i>No!</i>

26
00:01:00,852 --> 00:01:02,187
[Diego] <i>Because of what he did,</i>

27
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:04,898
<i>it's like he paid for all the crimes</i>
<i>he committed.</i>

28
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,941
<i>He will never hurt anyone again.</i>

29
00:01:07,025 --> 00:01:08,860
[gunshots]

30
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:11,029
[Julio] <i>I'm coming for you!</i>

31
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:14,741
<i>I will be coming for each</i>
<i>and every one of you!</i>

32
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:17,452
[Lily] <i>Arnaldo's death</i>
<i>just goes to show that</i>

33
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:19,871
<i>whether you're rich or poor,</i>

34
00:01:19,954 --> 00:01:21,372
<i>powerful or weak,</i>

35
00:01:21,456 --> 00:01:23,833
<i>what you do to others</i>

36
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:25,168
<i>will always come back to you.</i>

37
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:27,670
[Julio] <i>Rest now, my prince,</i>

38
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:32,425
<i>for I will burn the whole town</i>
<i>of Ardiente to ashes</i>

39
00:01:32,509 --> 00:01:34,636
<i>to avenge your death.</i>

40
00:01:34,719 --> 00:01:36,971
-[Diego] <i>Get away from there!</i>
-[explosion]

41
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:40,266
<i>Snap out of your insanity!</i>

42
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:42,477
<i>Help me and your son, Arnaldo!</i>

43
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:44,437
<i>Make them pay! They killed me!</i>

44
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:47,649
<i>Wake up, Ma! Wake up!</i>

45
00:01:50,151 --> 00:01:51,111
[Edna] This way, sir.

46
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:52,821
What's taking Ronald so long?

47
00:01:52,904 --> 00:01:54,489
Where is he?

48
00:01:54,572 --> 00:01:55,573
I have no idea.

49
00:01:56,074 --> 00:01:58,243
But I really hope he finds the Torillos.

50
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:00,370
Don't worry.

51
00:02:00,453 --> 00:02:02,122
He knows we're supposed to meet.

52
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:03,832
Let's just wait.

53
00:02:03,915 --> 00:02:06,209
[Efren] Let's just start
planning our next move.

54
00:02:06,292 --> 00:02:07,460
-[Ronald] Everyone.
-He's here.

55
00:02:07,544 --> 00:02:08,670
Ronald.

56
00:02:08,753 --> 00:02:09,963
It's confirmed.

57
00:02:10,046 --> 00:02:12,549
I've found Lily and Diego Torillo's house.

58
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:15,301
This is our chance.

59
00:02:16,302 --> 00:02:18,221
But we still don't know
what they're planning.

60
00:02:53,631 --> 00:02:56,384
[ominous music]

61
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:01,139
Pleased to meet you.

62
00:03:05,226 --> 00:03:06,436
I've been wanting to meet

63
00:03:06,519 --> 00:03:08,313
Red Dragon's daughter for so long.

64
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:10,732
The pleasure is mine.

65
00:03:15,403 --> 00:03:18,740
My mother gave me the password
to the Triad database.

66
00:03:18,823 --> 00:03:20,700
She gave this to me before she died.

67
00:03:26,915 --> 00:03:28,416
[suspenseful music]

68
00:03:50,063 --> 00:03:52,148
She also left me in charge
of the syndicate.

69
00:03:52,815 --> 00:03:54,525
I'll need all your support,

70
00:03:54,609 --> 00:03:56,903
so Papa and I can revive it.

71
00:04:12,502 --> 00:04:13,795
What do you need from us?

72
00:04:19,342 --> 00:04:21,177
I need your three G's.

73
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:24,180
Guns, goons, and gold.

74
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:27,600
I want lots of it.

75
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:41,781
This is their house. Leave it to me.

76
00:04:41,864 --> 00:04:45,868
Sir, my companions are hoping
to talk to Diego and Miss Lily.

77
00:04:46,035 --> 00:04:48,746
I'm sorry, but we don't know
who your companions are.

78
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,665
But they have something
important to tell them.

79
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:52,875
Can you just tell them we're outside?

80
00:04:52,959 --> 00:04:53,876
[Fernan] It's important.

81
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:55,837
We wouldn't have come here if--

82
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,338
Diego! Miss Lily!

83
00:04:57,922 --> 00:04:59,590
Good evening.

84
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:01,759
These people are looking for you.

85
00:05:01,843 --> 00:05:03,928
They say they have
something important to tell you.

86
00:05:11,769 --> 00:05:14,147
-Okay, let them in.
-Thank you, sir.

87
00:05:14,439 --> 00:05:15,481
Please come in.

88
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:17,233
Come. I told you so.

89
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:19,319
You wouldn't even let us in.

90
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:22,238
[Fernan] Here they are.

91
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:23,531
What brings you here?

92
00:05:23,614 --> 00:05:26,492
We're the relatives
of the Ardientes' victims.

93
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:30,163
We don't believe the accusations
Julio made against you.

94
00:05:30,788 --> 00:05:32,498
We want to help you fight them.

95
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:36,502
[pensive music playing]

96
00:05:53,144 --> 00:05:56,230
[Ronald] Our parents were
newspaper columnists.

97
00:05:59,317 --> 00:06:01,652
We were still kids when
the Ardientes had them abducted.

98
00:06:03,821 --> 00:06:05,698
<i>-Let go of me!</i>
<i>-Mom!</i>

99
00:06:07,617 --> 00:06:09,660
<i>-Mom! Mom!</i>
<i>-Edna!</i>

100
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:11,412
<i>Mom!</i>

101
00:06:11,496 --> 00:06:13,206
<i>Edna! No!</i>

102
00:06:13,289 --> 00:06:14,582
<i>-Mom!</i>
<i>-Kids…</i>

103
00:06:14,665 --> 00:06:16,125
<i>-Get up! Move!</i>
<i>-…we'll come back.</i>

104
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:17,251
<i>Edna!</i>

105
00:06:17,335 --> 00:06:19,295
<i>-Dad!</i>
<i>-Ronald!</i>

106
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:21,089
<i>-Kids!</i>
<i>-Mom!</i>

107
00:06:21,172 --> 00:06:24,634
<i>-Hurry up!</i>
<i>-My children! We'll come back!</i>

108
00:06:24,717 --> 00:06:27,178
<i>-Ronald!</i>
<i>-We'll come back!</i>

109
00:06:28,387 --> 00:06:30,098
<i>Mom!</i>

110
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:31,349
<i>Dad!</i>

111
00:06:35,853 --> 00:06:37,563
<i>-Don't take them!</i>
<i>-Mom!</i>

112
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:39,190
<i>Mom!</i>

113
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:42,735
We never saw them again.

114
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:45,238
We believe they were murdered after that.

115
00:06:46,364 --> 00:06:48,199
But we weren't able to file a case

116
00:06:48,282 --> 00:06:50,076
because we couldn't find their bodies.

117
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:52,453
They took care of any evidence

118
00:06:52,537 --> 00:06:54,122
that could implicate the Ardientes.

119
00:06:55,706 --> 00:06:56,666
[woman] <i>Shush now.</i>

120
00:06:56,749 --> 00:06:58,334
[Edna] <i>We left the country fearing</i>

121
00:06:58,417 --> 00:06:59,836
<i>the Ardientes would come for us next.</i>

122
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:02,004
<i>So, kids, are you ready?</i>

123
00:07:02,421 --> 00:07:03,506
<i>Yes.</i>

124
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:05,550
<i>Help me put their luggage in the car.</i>

125
00:07:07,176 --> 00:07:09,428
[Edna] <i>We tried starting anew,</i>

126
00:07:09,512 --> 00:07:10,930
<i>and left our past behind.</i>

127
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:13,266
<i>Let's go.</i>

128
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:21,482
But, then, we saw you on TV.

129
00:07:23,734 --> 00:07:26,362
[Ronald] <i>We saw how you</i>
<i>fought the Ardientes.</i>

130
00:07:26,988 --> 00:07:29,240
<i>Then, all the bad memories</i>
<i>came flooding back.</i>

131
00:07:30,491 --> 00:07:32,535
<i>Those Ardientes are despicable.</i>

132
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:35,204
<i>They're rotten to the core.</i>

133
00:07:36,414 --> 00:07:37,874
<i>We have to go back.</i>

134
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:39,917
[Edna] <i>We could no longer turn our backs</i>

135
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:41,544
<i>on what was happening back home.</i>

136
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:45,256
That's why we came back.

137
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:48,050
We met up with the relatives
of their other victims.

138
00:07:49,135 --> 00:07:51,095
<i>Edna, this is Efren.</i>

139
00:07:51,846 --> 00:07:53,973
<i>His family was one of Ardientes' victims.</i>

140
00:07:54,765 --> 00:07:55,892
<i>Please take a seat.</i>

141
00:07:56,434 --> 00:07:58,352
<i>-I'm Edna.</i>
<i>-My name's Efren.</i>

142
00:07:58,436 --> 00:08:00,521
<i>The others should be here soon.</i>

143
00:08:05,985 --> 00:08:07,403
<i>Oh, here they are.</i>

144
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:09,614
<i>This is Mister Ben and Mrs. Gloria.</i>

145
00:08:09,697 --> 00:08:11,032
<i>-Ben.</i>
<i>-Hi, I'm Ronald.</i>

146
00:08:11,115 --> 00:08:12,116
<i>I'm Efren.</i>

147
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,618
<i>-I'm Ronald.</i>
<i>-Hey, nice to meet you.</i>

148
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:29,509
We want to fight back.

149
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:33,638
All of us here have relatives,

150
00:08:33,721 --> 00:08:35,556
friends, and loved ones

151
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:37,767
who are still missing

152
00:08:37,850 --> 00:08:40,102
ever since the Ardientes
took them away from us.

153
00:08:41,979 --> 00:08:43,356
Hold on.

154
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:45,942
They've done even worse things
to the rest of us.

155
00:08:46,442 --> 00:08:50,446
At least Ronald and Edna here
still have each other.

156
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:51,447
What about me?

157
00:08:52,031 --> 00:08:55,409
The Ardientes had my wife, my child,

158
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:56,661
and even my parents killed.

159
00:08:57,161 --> 00:08:58,955
They took everyone in my life away.

160
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:01,541
They ruined my life.

161
00:09:06,796 --> 00:09:08,506
[Gloria] Just like you, Miss Lily,

162
00:09:08,839 --> 00:09:12,885
we're all looking for justice
for our loved ones.

163
00:09:13,427 --> 00:09:15,930
We need to find out what happened to them.

164
00:09:22,353 --> 00:09:24,438
Since we're all victims here,

165
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:25,898
we will help each other out.

166
00:09:27,191 --> 00:09:30,236
My family and I promise…

167
00:09:31,153 --> 00:09:34,740
to help you all look for
your missing loved ones.

168
00:09:34,991 --> 00:09:36,409
We've heard rumors.

169
00:09:37,493 --> 00:09:39,954
Apparently, the Ardientes have
a mass grave hidden somewhere.

170
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:43,499
A place where they bury
most of their victims.

171
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:48,796
Miss Lily, our parents
might be buried there.

172
00:09:48,879 --> 00:09:50,464
[tense music playing]

173
00:09:55,344 --> 00:09:57,346
[ominous music]

174
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,327
Hi, Papa.

175
00:10:20,494 --> 00:10:22,204
Your favorite daughter is back.

176
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:27,335
And, by the way, I've already
gained the Triad's support.

177
00:10:27,668 --> 00:10:29,378
[suspenseful music playing]

178
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:32,673
Welcome home.

179
00:10:33,924 --> 00:10:36,302
You know, I knew somehow

180
00:10:36,385 --> 00:10:38,679
you'd be able to get back on your feet.

181
00:10:38,763 --> 00:10:41,432
Oh, Papa, spare me this nonsense.

182
00:10:41,682 --> 00:10:44,602
Do you think I've forgotten
the things you've done?

183
00:10:45,227 --> 00:10:47,563
I swear on my mother, husband, and my son,

184
00:10:48,064 --> 00:10:49,357
I will fight this with you.

185
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:53,152
But this time around,
you will treat me as your equal.

186
00:10:54,195 --> 00:10:56,530
Whatever you want, my dear daughter.

187
00:10:57,740 --> 00:11:00,034
All I want is my revenge.

188
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:03,954
Good. Since we're on the same page.

189
00:11:04,038 --> 00:11:06,082
Now, I want the ugly heads

190
00:11:06,165 --> 00:11:08,334
of Diego and Lily Torillo.

191
00:11:28,938 --> 00:11:31,399
Do you still think they can help us?

192
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:33,943
Where is this fight headed, anyway?

193
00:11:34,026 --> 00:11:38,114
Ben, no one can help us except Lily Cruz!

194
00:11:38,197 --> 00:11:41,200
She's right, Ben. Let's trust Lily Cruz.

195
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:43,119
Lily Cruz?

196
00:11:43,202 --> 00:11:45,454
What if the Ardientes find out about this?

197
00:11:46,205 --> 00:11:49,375
Can Lily Cruz protect us?

198
00:11:49,458 --> 00:11:52,586
If not, we'll be tossed into
that mass grave too.

199
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:55,506
We're taking this risk for our loved ones.

200
00:11:56,715 --> 00:11:58,509
But this is a fight we can't win!

201
00:11:58,592 --> 00:12:00,511
We'll just end up dead
like the rest of them!

202
00:12:00,594 --> 00:12:01,595
-Ben!
-Ben.

203
00:12:01,679 --> 00:12:04,265
We're in this together,
and we will find a way.

204
00:12:04,348 --> 00:12:06,517
-[woman] He's right.
-Have some faith.

205
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:09,603
We're risking our lives
so we can finally get justice.

206
00:12:09,687 --> 00:12:12,273
-That's true.
-Yes, Ben. Calm down.

207
00:12:12,356 --> 00:12:14,483
We need to be united, not divided.

208
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:15,860
Sure.

209
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:16,986
Keep fooling yourselves,

210
00:12:17,069 --> 00:12:19,029
and believe you'll get justice!

211
00:12:19,113 --> 00:12:21,991
But I'm not getting my hopes up
for nothing again!

212
00:12:22,658 --> 00:12:25,077
I don't want to experience
the Ardientes' cruelty again!

213
00:12:26,662 --> 00:12:27,788
What?

214
00:12:28,205 --> 00:12:29,165
-Ben.
-Ben.

215
00:12:30,332 --> 00:12:31,208
So much for solidarity.

216
00:12:33,502 --> 00:12:36,797
Maybe we can still change his mind.

217
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:38,549
We just need to talk to him.

218
00:12:38,632 --> 00:12:40,593
[tense music playing]

219
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:49,393
[Lily] Based on the records,

220
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:53,272
Ronald and Edna's parents
were last seen in this area.

221
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:57,860
This is where the other victims
were last seen.

222
00:12:57,943 --> 00:13:01,071
Most of the rumors point
to this area as the mass grave.

223
00:13:02,907 --> 00:13:04,825
That's around one kilometer
away from here.

224
00:13:06,577 --> 00:13:09,371
Even if it takes us months,
years, or decades,

225
00:13:09,955 --> 00:13:12,124
we will find that mass grave.

226
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:13,751
We will find the victims

227
00:13:13,834 --> 00:13:15,961
and help the loved ones they left behind.

228
00:13:17,087 --> 00:13:20,174
The Ardientes will pay for their crimes.

229
00:13:20,257 --> 00:13:22,968
That's why we need to find
the mass grave soon.

230
00:13:41,695 --> 00:13:43,155
-Papa.
-[loads gun]

231
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:46,700
I gave you the men, the guns,
and everything else you need.

232
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:49,870
Why are Diego and Lily still alive?

233
00:13:49,954 --> 00:13:50,955
Are you up to it?

234
00:13:51,038 --> 00:13:53,999
Or is old age making you soft,
and you're ready for retirement?

235
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:56,293
Just tell me, and I'll get
the job done myself.

236
00:13:56,377 --> 00:13:57,503
[chuckles]

237
00:13:58,963 --> 00:14:03,175
The battle has already been won, Emilia.

238
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:09,557
Their names are already written
in the obituary.

239
00:14:10,599 --> 00:14:12,059
I'm just waiting…

240
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:15,896
for the right time to strike.

241
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:17,982
The time is now, Papa.

242
00:14:18,065 --> 00:14:19,984
I'll finish this once and for all.

243
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:22,069
Emilia…

244
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:27,324
you do not give orders
to the captain of the ship.

245
00:14:27,408 --> 00:14:29,368
Oh, correction, Papa.

246
00:14:29,869 --> 00:14:32,621
I am the co-captain of the ship, remember?

247
00:14:32,705 --> 00:14:34,164
We had an agreement.

248
00:14:34,248 --> 00:14:36,083
If it wasn't for me, Papa,

249
00:14:36,166 --> 00:14:38,961
this ship would have sunk a long time ago.

250
00:14:39,461 --> 00:14:41,505
[Emilia sighs]
It's useless talking to you.

251
00:14:51,098 --> 00:14:53,767
We're going to the families
of the victims.

252
00:14:53,851 --> 00:14:55,352
We're going to protect them.

253
00:14:55,436 --> 00:14:57,730
Then Mom and I will head to the site.

254
00:14:58,105 --> 00:15:00,232
We might find the mass grave there.

255
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:02,526
[Camia] We can't wait any longer.

256
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:06,739
We need to act before Julio
finds out what we're up to.

257
00:15:10,117 --> 00:15:12,077
-Be careful.
-You too.

258
00:15:13,203 --> 00:15:15,831
If only I could stay by your side,

259
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:17,458
so I could protect you, I would.

260
00:15:19,293 --> 00:15:20,210
But, you're right.

261
00:15:20,294 --> 00:15:22,421
This fight is bigger than both of us.

262
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:24,298
We're helping so many people.

263
00:15:24,381 --> 00:15:27,760
This will be the biggest case
Julio Ardiente will face

264
00:15:27,843 --> 00:15:29,219
if we find that mass grave.

265
00:15:30,512 --> 00:15:31,972
He will pay for his crimes.

266
00:15:33,807 --> 00:15:34,808
We'll take him down.

267
00:15:36,518 --> 00:15:38,604
Just remember our promise
to each other, Diego.

268
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:40,940
No one leaves…

269
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:43,609
…and no one gets left behind.

270
00:15:57,247 --> 00:15:58,248
Governor.

271
00:15:59,375 --> 00:16:00,459
He's here.

272
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:04,046
Let him in.

273
00:16:10,636 --> 00:16:13,555
[ominous music building]

274
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:21,105
Have a seat.

275
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:30,406
What did you want to tell me
about Lily and Diego?

276
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:34,451
Show me the money first.

277
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:37,955
Magbanua.

278
00:16:57,016 --> 00:16:59,518
Twenty million pesos.

279
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:04,231
As agreed upon, for your service.

280
00:17:05,774 --> 00:17:06,817
Now…

281
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:09,403
tell me what you know.

282
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:13,782
Lily and Diego know about the mass grave.

283
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:17,369
They're planning to expose

284
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:19,913
the hundreds of people
your family has killed.

285
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:22,624
[laughs]

286
00:17:26,045 --> 00:17:27,087
Truth is, Ben…

287
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:31,717
The only time they'll see that mass grave…

288
00:17:33,927 --> 00:17:37,389
is when I drop their corpses

289
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:40,059
down that pit.

290
00:17:40,768 --> 00:17:43,437
Only then will they find the mass grave.

291
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:46,190
But, before that happens…

292
00:17:47,941 --> 00:17:53,238
I will make them pay
for what they did to Arnaldo.

293
00:17:54,865 --> 00:17:55,866
Magbanua.

294
00:17:56,283 --> 00:17:57,701
Prepare our men.

295
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:02,539
I want the people of Ardiente to witness…

296
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:07,669
just how I'll mete out my punishment

297
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:09,671
and wrath on Lily and Diego.

298
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:13,801
[ominous music]

299
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:29,149
Villanueva, you're in charge of
protecting Lily and her mother.

300
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:31,568
Make sure nothing happens to them.

301
00:18:31,652 --> 00:18:32,569
Yes, sir.

302
00:18:33,153 --> 00:18:34,530
We'll get going.

303
00:18:35,489 --> 00:18:36,990
Anna, Marlon.

304
00:18:37,616 --> 00:18:38,742
Please be careful.

305
00:18:44,331 --> 00:18:46,583
Anna, Marlon, let's go.

306
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:47,918
Okay.

307
00:18:50,879 --> 00:18:51,880
Anna.

308
00:18:53,882 --> 00:18:54,883
What's wrong?

309
00:18:55,759 --> 00:18:58,720
I don't know if I should
text Jepoy or not.

310
00:18:59,012 --> 00:19:01,140
He might be able to help us.

311
00:19:02,057 --> 00:19:04,852
If he wanted to help,
he would be here by now.

312
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:07,771
And stop relying on people who don't care.

313
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:09,773
You should rely on the
people who are here.

314
00:19:11,275 --> 00:19:15,737
[soft music playing]

315
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:19,324
Let's go?

316
00:19:27,332 --> 00:19:28,876
[sensual music]

317
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:40,262
I love you, Madrigal.

318
00:19:41,305 --> 00:19:42,931
I love you so much.

319
00:19:45,517 --> 00:19:47,269
I love you too, Anna.

320
00:19:50,647 --> 00:19:51,648
What?!

321
00:19:52,983 --> 00:19:54,318
What did you just say?

322
00:19:57,321 --> 00:19:58,822
Did you just say "Anna"?

323
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:01,325
Huh?!

324
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:03,785
Did you say "Anna"?

325
00:20:04,912 --> 00:20:06,371
[stammers] I'm sorry.

326
00:20:07,497 --> 00:20:08,457
Sorry, Natalie.

327
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:09,625
-[shouts]
-Ouch.

328
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:11,752
-Ouch. Sorry! Sorry!
-[Natalie groaning]

329
00:20:11,835 --> 00:20:13,212
[Natalie cries]

330
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:14,296
Natalie!

331
00:20:14,713 --> 00:20:15,714
Hey, Natalie.

332
00:20:16,048 --> 00:20:17,216
I'm sorry.

333
00:20:19,051 --> 00:20:20,552
-I'm sorry.
-[continues crying]

334
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:22,346
Natalie.

335
00:20:24,264 --> 00:20:25,849
That's my name.

336
00:20:29,019 --> 00:20:31,647
Do you want me
to spell out my name for you?

337
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:34,316
It's…

338
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:36,068
N.

339
00:20:36,777 --> 00:20:37,653
A.

340
00:20:38,695 --> 00:20:39,863
T.

341
00:20:40,864 --> 00:20:41,823
A.

342
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:43,075
L.

343
00:20:44,743 --> 00:20:45,744
I.

344
00:20:46,536 --> 00:20:47,537
E.

345
00:20:50,165 --> 00:20:54,127
Do you want me to carve…

346
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,256
each letter on your skin…

347
00:20:58,507 --> 00:21:01,593
so that you won't forget my name?

348
00:21:02,052 --> 00:21:03,512
I'm sorry.

349
00:21:03,595 --> 00:21:05,389
Get out!

350
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:07,182
Get out!

351
00:21:16,316 --> 00:21:17,734
Get out!

352
00:21:18,527 --> 00:21:19,778
Get out!

353
00:21:20,904 --> 00:21:22,572
[Natalie grunts, cries]

354
00:21:24,116 --> 00:21:25,450
Get out!

355
00:21:32,457 --> 00:21:35,419
[soft music playing]

356
00:21:46,430 --> 00:21:49,016
[grunting]

357
00:22:06,116 --> 00:22:07,576
I really love you, Anna.

358
00:22:12,831 --> 00:22:13,915
I need to see you.

359
00:22:16,626 --> 00:22:17,753
I need to see you.

360
00:22:19,504 --> 00:22:22,049
[soft music continues]

361
00:22:34,436 --> 00:22:37,147
[tense music playing]

362
00:22:41,068 --> 00:22:43,653
The mass grave could be around here.

363
00:22:43,737 --> 00:22:45,155
We'll check this area.

364
00:22:49,493 --> 00:22:52,329
[ominous music playing]

365
00:23:17,771 --> 00:23:18,814
Lily?

366
00:23:20,941 --> 00:23:21,942
Anna?

367
00:23:23,693 --> 00:23:24,611
Anna?

368
00:23:29,616 --> 00:23:30,617
Anna!

369
00:23:32,327 --> 00:23:33,328
Anna!

370
00:23:35,330 --> 00:23:36,665
Where is everyone?

371
00:23:40,585 --> 00:23:41,878
-Lily?
-[door opens]

372
00:23:45,257 --> 00:23:46,758
Where are Anna and Lily?

373
00:23:46,842 --> 00:23:49,803
They went to see the relatives
of the Ardientes' victims.

374
00:23:52,264 --> 00:23:54,349
Tell me where they are.

375
00:23:57,894 --> 00:23:58,937
[Gloria] Ronald.

376
00:23:59,479 --> 00:24:01,982
Is it true they finally found
the mass grave?

377
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:05,068
Lily Cruz thinks she knows where it is.

378
00:24:05,152 --> 00:24:06,611
They're going there right now.

379
00:24:07,487 --> 00:24:10,866
I called you all here today
to ask for help.

380
00:24:11,283 --> 00:24:12,409
What are we waiting for?

381
00:24:12,826 --> 00:24:13,702
Let's go.

382
00:24:13,785 --> 00:24:14,995
So we can finally expose

383
00:24:15,078 --> 00:24:17,414
what those Ardientes did
to our loved ones.

384
00:24:17,497 --> 00:24:19,124
-That's right.
-Right.

385
00:24:19,207 --> 00:24:20,667
Hold on.

386
00:24:21,209 --> 00:24:23,879
What if they come back for us?

387
00:24:24,838 --> 00:24:26,673
How long are we just going to hide?

388
00:24:27,048 --> 00:24:29,259
It's time for us to fight the Ardientes.

389
00:24:29,342 --> 00:24:30,260
That's right.

390
00:24:30,343 --> 00:24:33,513
Friends, Ronald and Edna are right.

391
00:24:34,639 --> 00:24:37,184
It's time for us
to stand up to the Ardientes.

392
00:24:37,267 --> 00:24:38,393
[Ronald] That's right.

393
00:24:38,894 --> 00:24:40,478
-Everything will be fine.
-Have faith.

394
00:24:41,521 --> 00:24:42,522
[indistinct]

395
00:24:44,107 --> 00:24:46,902
[tense music playing]

396
00:25:02,918 --> 00:25:05,003
You guys stay here.

397
00:25:06,004 --> 00:25:06,963
Stand guard.

398
00:25:07,047 --> 00:25:08,006
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

399
00:25:08,089 --> 00:25:09,132
Let's go.

400
00:25:09,633 --> 00:25:11,301
[tense music playing]

401
00:25:14,012 --> 00:25:16,264
-[door kicked open]
-[people exclaim]

402
00:25:16,348 --> 00:25:18,141
What's this?! What's going on here?!

403
00:25:18,225 --> 00:25:19,226
[screams]

404
00:25:19,768 --> 00:25:21,269
What's the meaning of this?

405
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:24,231
[goon] Don't resist, and do what we say.

406
00:25:24,314 --> 00:25:26,191
Who called this meeting?!

407
00:25:27,275 --> 00:25:28,235
Answer me!

408
00:25:28,318 --> 00:25:30,862
Are you plotting something
against the Ardientes?

409
00:25:31,696 --> 00:25:32,697
Idiots.

410
00:25:34,783 --> 00:25:35,825
What are you waiting for?

411
00:25:36,576 --> 00:25:37,535
Take them.

412
00:25:37,619 --> 00:25:38,745
-Get up!
-Hurry!

413
00:25:38,828 --> 00:25:40,413
-Hurry up!
-Quick!

414
00:25:41,331 --> 00:25:42,791
-Get up!
-Hurry! Get up!

415
00:25:42,874 --> 00:25:44,125
You! Get up!

416
00:25:44,417 --> 00:25:46,044
Go out right now!

417
00:25:50,382 --> 00:25:51,716
Wait. Hold on.

418
00:25:52,884 --> 00:25:54,928
[tense music continues]

419
00:25:56,763 --> 00:25:58,765
Those are the Ardientes' men.

420
00:26:01,268 --> 00:26:02,894
Batch, come with me.

421
00:26:02,978 --> 00:26:04,688
-Okay.
-Anna, you stay here.

422
00:26:04,771 --> 00:26:06,564
No matter what happens, just stay here.

423
00:26:07,899 --> 00:26:09,067
Keep Anna safe.

424
00:26:10,485 --> 00:26:11,569
Be careful.

425
00:26:11,653 --> 00:26:12,654
We will.

426
00:26:24,666 --> 00:26:25,709
[Diego] Batch.

427
00:26:33,508 --> 00:26:34,718
Batch, they aren't looking.

428
00:27:04,080 --> 00:27:05,373
Where are those two?

429
00:27:05,457 --> 00:27:06,541
They were just here.

430
00:27:07,042 --> 00:27:08,001
Come on. Let's look for them!

431
00:27:08,084 --> 00:27:09,169
-Let's go.
-Take that side.

432
00:27:10,920 --> 00:27:13,340
[tense music intensifies]

433
00:27:24,392 --> 00:27:26,394
Batch, take this.

434
00:27:28,897 --> 00:27:30,315
Get them all down there!

435
00:27:30,398 --> 00:27:31,483
Go! Go!

436
00:27:32,025 --> 00:27:32,984
Move it!

437
00:27:34,069 --> 00:27:36,404
-[goon 1] Go down!
-[goon 2] Take them! Hurry!

438
00:27:36,488 --> 00:27:37,489
[goon 2] Go down!

439
00:27:40,950 --> 00:27:41,951
[goon 1] Come on!

440
00:27:43,495 --> 00:27:45,372
-Move faster!
-So slow! Hurry!

441
00:27:45,455 --> 00:27:47,624
-On your knees! Hurry!
-Faster! Faster!

442
00:27:47,707 --> 00:27:48,792
-Get down!
-Hurry!

443
00:27:49,376 --> 00:27:50,418
Get down!

444
00:27:50,502 --> 00:27:51,920
I said get down!

445
00:27:52,379 --> 00:27:53,755
Thought you could get away?

446
00:27:54,506 --> 00:27:56,716
-Where are the guards?!
-On the ground!

447
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:58,176
Where are the men I stationed here?!

448
00:27:58,259 --> 00:27:59,511
[goon 3] Boss, we can't find them!

449
00:28:03,890 --> 00:28:06,351
[tense music intensifies]

450
00:28:16,861 --> 00:28:18,238
-Batch.
-Come on. Let's go.

451
00:28:18,321 --> 00:28:19,989
-One. Two.
-Two.

452
00:28:20,073 --> 00:28:21,074
[both] Three.

453
00:28:25,203 --> 00:28:26,329
[grunts]

454
00:28:26,413 --> 00:28:28,915
[gunfire]

455
00:28:35,839 --> 00:28:37,549
-[clamoring]
-[gunfire continues]

456
00:28:42,512 --> 00:28:44,889
-Ma'am, wait here!
-No! We need to help them!

457
00:28:45,140 --> 00:28:46,766
[gunfire continues]

458
00:28:50,437 --> 00:28:51,479
Anna?

459
00:28:52,188 --> 00:28:54,190
-[gunfire continues]
-[people clamoring]

460
00:29:06,286 --> 00:29:07,245
[gunfire continues]

461
00:29:09,873 --> 00:29:10,915
[women exclaiming]

462
00:29:15,503 --> 00:29:16,421
Don't move.

463
00:29:21,760 --> 00:29:22,927
[action music playing]

464
00:29:36,691 --> 00:29:38,568
-They're getting away!
-Let's get them!

465
00:29:39,694 --> 00:29:41,070
[women speaking indistinctly]

466
00:29:41,154 --> 00:29:42,655
Where do you think you're going?

467
00:29:44,157 --> 00:29:45,700
Hey! Come back here!

468
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:48,286
Let go of me!

469
00:29:50,580 --> 00:29:51,581
[Anna groans]

470
00:29:57,670 --> 00:29:58,630
Let's finish her off!

471
00:29:58,713 --> 00:30:00,173
[suspenseful music]

472
00:30:04,093 --> 00:30:05,094
Anna!

473
00:30:15,063 --> 00:30:16,606
Anna! Anna! Anna.

474
00:30:19,609 --> 00:30:21,236
Rosanna. Anna!

475
00:30:22,278 --> 00:30:23,696
Anna! Anna!

476
00:30:24,739 --> 00:30:26,324
Anna! Anna!

477
00:30:26,574 --> 00:30:27,575
Anna!

478
00:30:28,243 --> 00:30:31,120
Anna! Anna! Anna!

479
00:30:31,204 --> 00:30:33,456
Rosanna Navarro. It's me, Jepoy.

480
00:30:33,540 --> 00:30:35,416
If you can hear me, I still love you.

481
00:30:37,126 --> 00:30:38,962
Anna. Rosanna!

482
00:30:39,921 --> 00:30:40,922
Rosanna.

483
00:30:41,464 --> 00:30:42,590
Rosanna, hey.

484
00:30:44,759 --> 00:30:45,760
Anna?

485
00:30:48,179 --> 00:30:50,390
[somber music playing]

486
00:30:57,063 --> 00:30:58,064
[Jepoy] Hey, Anna.

487
00:30:58,147 --> 00:31:00,066
Jepoy, I'll take it from here.

488
00:31:00,942 --> 00:31:03,069
Jepoy, come on.

489
00:31:03,486 --> 00:31:04,612
Anna.

490
00:31:04,696 --> 00:31:06,072
Anna, please wake up.

491
00:31:06,155 --> 00:31:07,240
Anna.

492
00:31:08,741 --> 00:31:09,742
[Marlon] Anna, wake up.

493
00:31:10,869 --> 00:31:11,744
Anna.

494
00:31:14,330 --> 00:31:15,582
Anna, it's me, Marlon.

495
00:31:16,499 --> 00:31:17,500
Anna.

496
00:31:18,877 --> 00:31:19,919
Anna.

497
00:31:21,087 --> 00:31:22,130
Go ahead.

498
00:31:24,340 --> 00:31:25,383
Anna.

499
00:31:28,136 --> 00:31:29,178
[Marlon whispers] Anna.

500
00:31:30,096 --> 00:31:32,599
[somber music continues]

501
00:31:38,605 --> 00:31:39,606
Are you okay?

502
00:31:40,899 --> 00:31:42,525
Anna, are you okay?

503
00:31:53,536 --> 00:31:54,537
Are you okay?

504
00:32:04,756 --> 00:32:07,091
[tense music playing]

505
00:32:19,354 --> 00:32:20,313
[tires screech]

506
00:32:26,861 --> 00:32:27,946
[gunshot]

507
00:32:29,322 --> 00:32:30,323
[Camia gasps]

508
00:32:31,449 --> 00:32:32,659
-Duck!
-[Camia yelps]

509
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:37,705
[gunfire continues]

510
00:32:46,381 --> 00:32:47,298
Mom, our guns.

511
00:32:49,133 --> 00:32:50,843
[tense music continues]

512
00:32:57,433 --> 00:32:58,226
Mom, hurry.

513
00:32:59,852 --> 00:33:01,187
[Lily] Take my mother away from here.

514
00:33:01,270 --> 00:33:02,855
Get away from here! Go to Diego.

515
00:33:02,939 --> 00:33:04,691
Tell him Julio's men ambushed us.

516
00:33:04,774 --> 00:33:05,984
Lily, I can't just leave you here.

517
00:33:06,067 --> 00:33:07,443
Mom, please, you're our only hope.

518
00:33:07,527 --> 00:33:08,861
I'll be right behind you.

519
00:33:08,945 --> 00:33:10,571
All right. I promise
I'll come back for you.

520
00:33:10,655 --> 00:33:12,865
-I love you so much.
-[gunshots]

521
00:33:12,949 --> 00:33:14,659
Hurry! Get my mother out of here!

522
00:33:33,469 --> 00:33:36,347
[dramatic music]

523
00:33:47,900 --> 00:33:50,361
[music intensifies]

524
00:34:09,547 --> 00:34:11,966
-[Camia yelps]
-[gunshots]

525
00:34:26,898 --> 00:34:30,234
<i>Arnaldo, I want to clear a path</i>

526
00:34:30,318 --> 00:34:31,527
<i>for your comeback.</i>

527
00:34:32,528 --> 00:34:36,491
<i>So that you can fulfill</i>
<i>all of your lifelong dreams.</i>

528
00:34:37,075 --> 00:34:39,077
<i>And let's face it.</i>

529
00:34:39,494 --> 00:34:40,953
<i>Let's face the truth.</i>

530
00:34:41,037 --> 00:34:43,456
<i>Age is creeping up on me.</i>

531
00:34:43,539 --> 00:34:48,920
<i>And I'm ready to turn over</i>
<i>the baton of leadership to you.</i>

532
00:34:49,003 --> 00:34:52,215
<i>I'll be the one carrying on</i>
<i>the family's legacy.</i>

533
00:34:53,257 --> 00:34:54,342
<i>I promise you that.</i>

534
00:34:55,384 --> 00:34:58,471
<i>And that has always been my dream.</i>

535
00:34:59,514 --> 00:35:00,932
<i>Thank you so much.</i>

536
00:35:01,432 --> 00:35:03,684
<i>-Viva Ardiente.</i>
<i>-Viva Ardiente.</i>

537
00:35:03,768 --> 00:35:05,144
-[glasses clink]
-[Julio chuckles]

538
00:35:06,687 --> 00:35:08,397
I remember…

539
00:35:10,316 --> 00:35:12,944
I used to have a drinking partner.

540
00:35:17,365 --> 00:35:19,242
Wherever you are, Arnaldo,

541
00:35:20,576 --> 00:35:21,786
cheers.

542
00:35:28,292 --> 00:35:29,168
[sighs]

543
00:35:42,306 --> 00:35:44,600
[phone rings]

544
00:35:48,146 --> 00:35:49,230
Yes?

545
00:35:49,939 --> 00:35:52,483
Governor, we have Lily Cruz.

546
00:35:54,402 --> 00:35:56,154
[chuckles]

547
00:35:58,322 --> 00:35:59,574
Yeah. Okay.

548
00:36:03,327 --> 00:36:04,745
[exhales, sniffles]

549
00:36:07,748 --> 00:36:08,833
[exhales]

550
00:36:09,792 --> 00:36:11,294
Lily Cruz…

551
00:36:14,172 --> 00:36:16,340
you're starting to bore me.

552
00:36:17,967 --> 00:36:20,887
It turns out, you're not as intelligent

553
00:36:20,970 --> 00:36:22,722
as I thought you were.

554
00:36:26,559 --> 00:36:28,477
You're either dumb…

555
00:36:30,354 --> 00:36:34,775
or you've got a handful of bodyguards…

556
00:36:35,693 --> 00:36:37,069
who are stupid.

557
00:36:38,905 --> 00:36:40,323
Just like that…

558
00:36:41,574 --> 00:36:44,869
my man, Magbanua, was able to get you?

559
00:36:46,913 --> 00:36:49,373
This is unforgivable.

560
00:36:52,084 --> 00:36:54,837
I expected more from you,

561
00:36:55,296 --> 00:36:56,589
Lily Cruz.

562
00:36:59,675 --> 00:37:02,720
<i>Death isn't enough</i>

563
00:37:02,803 --> 00:37:06,224
<i>to punish the people</i>
<i>who killed my grandson.</i>

564
00:37:08,184 --> 00:37:11,729
<i>What will be more satisfying</i>
<i>than their death</i>

565
00:37:12,313 --> 00:37:16,317
<i>is the suffering I will make them feel.</i>

566
00:37:19,028 --> 00:37:20,905
Big mistake, Lily Cruz.

567
00:37:23,324 --> 00:37:25,284
When you took the life…

568
00:37:26,702 --> 00:37:27,703
of Arnaldo.

569
00:37:29,247 --> 00:37:31,624
You think you know pain,

570
00:37:32,917 --> 00:37:34,085
Lily Cruz?

571
00:37:35,628 --> 00:37:38,130
You've never felt the kind of pain

572
00:37:38,214 --> 00:37:41,259
that I'm going to make you feel.

573
00:37:44,637 --> 00:37:49,934
Now you will feel the
wrath of Julio Ardiente.

574
00:37:50,434 --> 00:37:53,354
[suspenseful music]

575
00:38:07,285 --> 00:38:09,161
[Diego's phone rings]

576
00:38:10,162 --> 00:38:12,373
-[line ringing]
-[Camia panting]

577
00:38:15,918 --> 00:38:18,004
-[line ringing]
-[Camia panting]

578
00:38:19,797 --> 00:38:21,966
-Diego.
-[line ringing]

579
00:38:27,346 --> 00:38:30,182
[ominous music]

580
00:38:36,439 --> 00:38:38,899
Thank you for saving us, Diego.

581
00:38:39,567 --> 00:38:42,320
We're really grateful
that we're all safe and sound.

582
00:38:42,778 --> 00:38:46,490
We'll always be here to help you.

583
00:38:46,574 --> 00:38:48,909
[somber piano music]

584
00:39:06,260 --> 00:39:08,012
-Thank you very much.
-You're welcome.

585
00:39:11,557 --> 00:39:13,809
<i>Anna! Anna! Rosanna Navarro.</i>

586
00:39:15,311 --> 00:39:17,605
[soft music playing]

587
00:39:17,688 --> 00:39:18,606
Anna.

588
00:39:19,357 --> 00:39:20,524
Is there a problem?

589
00:39:21,942 --> 00:39:24,653
I heard you say my name earlier.

590
00:39:26,113 --> 00:39:27,948
I don't remember mentioning anything.

591
00:39:32,995 --> 00:39:35,414
So, you weren't the one who saved me.

592
00:39:42,004 --> 00:39:44,965
I saw you lying there
unconscious so I helped you.

593
00:39:46,592 --> 00:39:47,760
But you're right, Anna.

594
00:39:49,261 --> 00:39:50,554
I'm not the one who saved you.

595
00:39:53,349 --> 00:39:54,475
<i>Rosanna.</i>

596
00:39:54,850 --> 00:39:57,645
<i>Only two people know my real name.</i>

597
00:39:58,479 --> 00:40:00,106
<i>It's Lily and Jepoy.</i>

598
00:40:20,584 --> 00:40:22,461
[crowd chanting] Justice for the mayor!

599
00:40:22,545 --> 00:40:26,006
Justice for the mayor!
Justice for the mayor!

600
00:40:26,090 --> 00:40:30,803
[crowd continues chanting]

601
00:40:30,886 --> 00:40:33,514
Justice for the mayor!
Justice for the mayor!

602
00:40:33,597 --> 00:40:34,849
We're here to--

603
00:40:37,601 --> 00:40:40,271
Citizens of Poblacion Ardiente,

604
00:40:40,354 --> 00:40:42,314
do any of you believe…

605
00:40:43,274 --> 00:40:46,485
the claims of our vile enemies?

606
00:40:47,820 --> 00:40:51,949
That your beloved Mayor Arnaldo
killed himself?!

607
00:40:52,032 --> 00:40:53,659
[crowd chant] No! We don't believe them!

608
00:40:53,742 --> 00:40:55,911
We don't believe them!

609
00:40:55,995 --> 00:40:58,789
-They're all liars!
-It's not true!

610
00:40:58,873 --> 00:41:01,125
-Liars!
-We don't believe them!

611
00:41:01,208 --> 00:41:04,211
[man] Señor Julio,
we're here to support you!

612
00:41:04,503 --> 00:41:05,838
This is too much.

613
00:41:07,923 --> 00:41:09,592
My grandson's already dead.

614
00:41:11,969 --> 00:41:15,014
And they still want to ruin his image.

615
00:41:17,975 --> 00:41:20,102
Your mayor is gone.

616
00:41:21,604 --> 00:41:24,315
Yet, here they are, destroying his memory.

617
00:41:24,899 --> 00:41:26,233
They've gone too far.

618
00:41:27,276 --> 00:41:29,528
This is the last time they will hurt us.

619
00:41:33,365 --> 00:41:35,284
I only have one request.

620
00:41:37,578 --> 00:41:41,540
Let's all meet at the capitol.

621
00:41:42,374 --> 00:41:44,668
Call all your relatives.

622
00:41:44,752 --> 00:41:48,005
-[man] Let's go to the capitol.
-[Julio] Call your children.

623
00:41:48,088 --> 00:41:49,715
Call all your friends.

624
00:41:52,051 --> 00:41:53,802
Because today,

625
00:41:56,055 --> 00:41:58,516
we will get justice!

626
00:42:01,227 --> 00:42:04,939
Today, we will punish…

627
00:42:05,940 --> 00:42:07,608
the real criminal!

628
00:42:08,484 --> 00:42:12,321
The murderer who killed Mayor Arnaldo!

629
00:42:16,116 --> 00:42:17,576
On this day…

630
00:42:19,787 --> 00:42:21,413
we will punish…

631
00:42:22,581 --> 00:42:24,124
Lily Cruz!

632
00:42:24,208 --> 00:42:28,879
-Punish her!
-Justice for Mayor Arnaldo!

633
00:42:28,963 --> 00:42:32,967
[indistinct shouting]

634
00:42:36,929 --> 00:42:39,390
[crowd speaking indistinctly]

635
00:42:39,765 --> 00:42:43,352
[unintelligible]

636
00:42:44,103 --> 00:42:46,146
[crowd] Viva Ardiente!

637
00:42:48,899 --> 00:42:50,734
We're making sure the Ardientes' men

638
00:42:50,818 --> 00:42:52,570
won't be able to escape.

639
00:42:56,615 --> 00:42:58,284
You'll testify against the Ardientes,

640
00:42:59,076 --> 00:43:00,828
and admit they sent you here.

641
00:43:03,497 --> 00:43:05,624
You won't get anything from me.

642
00:43:08,002 --> 00:43:10,754
You know what?
You're just wasting your time.

643
00:43:11,380 --> 00:43:14,925
No one can ever defeat the Ardientes.

644
00:43:15,009 --> 00:43:17,428
Justice and truth will always prevail!

645
00:43:18,387 --> 00:43:20,222
You're only strengthening
our determination

646
00:43:20,306 --> 00:43:21,265
to fight the Ardientes!

647
00:43:21,348 --> 00:43:22,975
The truth will come out eventually.

648
00:43:23,058 --> 00:43:25,185
Everyone will discover how vile
the Ardientes truly are.

649
00:43:26,061 --> 00:43:29,481
Keep dreaming, because
the Ardientes are here to stay.

650
00:43:29,565 --> 00:43:32,943
[tense music playing]

651
00:43:59,261 --> 00:44:00,387
[Camia groans]

652
00:44:00,471 --> 00:44:02,056
[yelping]

653
00:44:03,641 --> 00:44:05,851
[yelps, groans]

654
00:44:09,063 --> 00:44:12,191
[tense music]

655
00:44:12,274 --> 00:44:14,068
[breathes heavily]

656
00:44:14,818 --> 00:44:17,363
[tense music playing]

657
00:44:32,836 --> 00:44:35,589
<i>-You killed him!</i>
<i>-Is it hard to accept, Julio?!</i>

658
00:44:35,673 --> 00:44:38,258
<i>Your beloved grandson killed himself</i>

659
00:44:38,342 --> 00:44:40,427
<i>because he couldn't stomach</i>
<i>being the monster…</i>

660
00:44:40,511 --> 00:44:42,429
-<i>…you turned him into!</i>
-[Julio shouts]

661
00:44:42,513 --> 00:44:43,597
[man] <i>Listen up, everyone!</i>

662
00:44:43,681 --> 00:44:46,141
<i>The governor wants us</i>
<i>to head over to the plaza.</i>

663
00:44:46,225 --> 00:44:48,811
<i>He said they will bring Lily Cruz there</i>
<i>and punish her</i>

664
00:44:48,894 --> 00:44:50,187
<i>for murdering our mayor!</i>

665
00:44:50,270 --> 00:44:52,356
<i>Let us show our support for the Ardientes!</i>

666
00:44:52,439 --> 00:44:54,983
<i>-We will be one…</i>
-[crowd] <i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

667
00:44:55,067 --> 00:44:58,737
[Julio] <i>Everyone, behold</i>
<i>the cancer afflicting this town.</i>

668
00:44:58,821 --> 00:44:59,905
<i>Lily Cruz!</i>

669
00:44:59,988 --> 00:45:02,449
-[indistinct shouting]
-[woman] <i>You killed our mayor!</i>

670
00:45:02,533 --> 00:45:05,577
<i>You're a murderer!</i>
<i>You deserve to be punished!</i>

671
00:45:05,661 --> 00:45:07,663
[theme music fades]
